Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Common/GPU: never block the render thread under Emscripten

Patch 0008 gave the GL loop back to the browser's event loop, and the port then
got as far as five animation frames before stopping again. What stops it is one
line inside the loop body: GLRenderManager::ThreadFrame() waits on a condition
variable until the emu thread pushes a task.

On every other platform the render thread is a thread of our own and that wait
is exactly right. Here the render thread is the browser's main thread, and a
blocking wait there is worse than slow. While the main thread sits in the wait
it is not servicing the proxy queue that Emscripten's worker threads use to
reach it — so a wait for the emu thread can be a wait on ourselves. Emscripten
says as much at runtime:

    Blocking on the main thread is very dangerous, see
    https://emscripten.org/docs/porting/pthreads.html#blocking-on-the-main-browser-thread

So under Emscripten an empty queue means there is no frame to run yet, and the
honest answer is to return and let the event loop turn. The caller is
emscripten_set_main_loop, so the question is asked again on the next animation
frame; a frame left partway through resumes where it stopped, since nothing else
touches GL in between.

Every other platform keeps the wait, and the change is confined to that one
branch.

diff --git a/Common/GPU/OpenGL/GLRenderManager.cpp b/Common/GPU/OpenGL/GLRenderManager.cpp
index e6385773a..c1f03084d 100644
--- a/Common/GPU/OpenGL/GLRenderManager.cpp
+++ b/Common/GPU/OpenGL/GLRenderManager.cpp
@@ -149,7 +149,23 @@ bool GLRenderManager::ThreadFrame() {
 		// to keep things uniform.
 		{
 			std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(pushMutex_);
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+			// The render thread is the browser's main thread, and it must not block.
+			// While it sits in this wait it is also not servicing the queue that worker
+			// threads use to reach it, so waiting here for the emu thread can be waiting
+			// on ourselves — and even when it is not, a main thread that does not return
+			// to the event loop presents no frame and answers no input.
+			//
+			// There is simply no work yet, so say so. The caller runs this from
+			// emscripten_set_main_loop, and will ask again on the next animation frame;
+			// a frame left half-run resumes exactly where it stopped, because nothing
+			// else touches GL in between.
+			if (renderThreadQueue_.empty()) {
+				return true;
+			}
+#else
 			pushCondVar_.wait(lock, [this] { return !renderThreadQueue_.empty(); });
+#endif
 			task = renderThreadQueue_.front();
 			renderThreadQueue_.pop();
 		}
